  "answer": "To determine if we are using all the latitude NERC provides for **CIP-010-4 Part 2.3**, I need to compare the standard's specific requirements against our internal procedures.\n\nThe standard for **Part 2.3** (which falls under the Configuration Monitoring requirements of **R2**) specifies a single, hardcoded interval:\n\n*   **The Standard's Requirement:** For High Impact BES Cyber Systems and their associated EACMS and PCA, we must monitor for changes to the baseline configuration **at least once every 35 calendar days** [csection-c3153294f86857a2f12d].\n\nTo answer your question, I need to check our internal documentation to see if we have narrowed this 35-day window to a more frequent or more rigid interval (e.g., \"every 30 days\" or \"weekly\"). \n\nI currently have the regulatory text, but I do not yet have our operator-side procedures or notes in this conversation to perform the comparison.\n\n**Would you like me to search our internal documents for our specific monitoring intervals for Part 2.3?**\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-c3153294f86857a2f12d (CIP-010-4 R2 Part 2.1 requirement text)",
